1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,646
Ab time hai Python se ek
model ke saath baat karne ka.

2
00:00:04,866 --> 00:00:10,060
Iss lesson mein hum pehle samjhenge
ki API kya hoti hai aur kyun hoti hai.

3
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:16,382
Phir API key ko safely set karenge,
official Anthropic SDK install karenge, pehla

4
00:00:16,382 --> 00:00:21,129
message bhejenge, aur response
ka har ek hissa kholke dekhenge.

5
00:00:22,429 --> 00:00:28,187
Iss lesson ke baad aap API ko ek
simple analogy ke saath explain kar paoge.

6
00:00:28,537 --> 00:00:32,296
API key ko safely create
aur store karna seekhoge.

7
00:00:32,646 --> 00:00:35,687
Messages dot create se request bhejoge.

8
00:00:36,037 --> 00:00:40,631
Aur response ko padhoge:
content blocks, stop reason, aur usage.

9
00:00:41,931 --> 00:00:43,776
Pehle what: API kya hai?

10
00:00:43,996 --> 00:00:46,100
Ek restaurant imagine karo.

11
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:48,680
Aap seedhe kitchen mein nahi jaate.

12
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:54,525
Aap waiter ko order dete ho, waiter
kitchen tak order le jaata hai, aur khana wapas

13
00:00:54,525 --> 00:00:55,203
laata hai.

14
00:00:55,553 --> 00:00:57,737
Aapka Python code customer hai.

15
00:00:57,957 --> 00:00:59,430
Order hai request.

16
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:01,354
API waiter hai.

17
00:01:01,574 --> 00:01:06,028
Waiter ke paas order lene ke
fixed rules hote hain, jaise menu.

18
00:01:06,378 --> 00:01:08,456
Aur model ke servers kitchen hain.

19
00:01:08,676 --> 00:01:11,619
Jo khana wapas aata hai, woh response hai.

20
00:01:11,969 --> 00:01:13,987
Ab why: API kyun hoti hai?

21
00:01:14,207 --> 00:01:18,961
Kyunki model bahut bade servers
par chalta hai, aapke laptop par nahi.

22
00:01:19,181 --> 00:01:25,329
API ek fixed, safe tareeka deti hai,
taaki koi bhi program un servers se baat kar

23
00:01:25,329 --> 00:01:25,708
sake.

24
00:01:27,008 --> 00:01:28,448
Ab API key.

25
00:01:28,668 --> 00:01:31,848
Pehle Claude Console
mein ek API key banao.

26
00:01:32,068 --> 00:01:36,470
Dhyan rahe, API ka billing
chat subscription se alag hota hai.

27
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:42,611
Phir usse ek environment variable mein
rakho, jiska naam hai ANTHROPIC API KEY.

28
00:01:42,831 --> 00:01:48,345
SDK isse automatically padh leta hai,
toh key aapke code mein kabhi nahi dikhti.

29
00:01:48,695 --> 00:01:53,346
Key ko kabhi code, chat,
screenshot, ya git commit mein paste mat karo.

30
00:01:53,566 --> 00:01:58,159
Agar key leak ho jaaye, toh turant
Console mein delete karo aur nayi banao.

31
00:01:58,509 --> 00:02:00,012
Abhi key nahi hai?

32
00:02:00,232 --> 00:02:01,595
Koi baat nahi.

33
00:02:01,815 --> 00:02:05,700
Iss module ka sab kuch
offline mode mein bhi chalta hai.

34
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,776
Woh abhi samjhati hoon.

35
00:02:09,076 --> 00:02:12,034
API key ko ATM PIN ki tarah socho.

36
00:02:12,254 --> 00:02:16,729
Jiske paas aapka PIN hai, woh
aapka paisa kharch kar sakta hai.

37
00:02:16,949 --> 00:02:22,416
Jiske paas aapki API key hai, woh
aapka API credit kharch kar sakta hai.

38
00:02:22,636 --> 00:02:25,386
Aap PIN card par likhkar nahi rakhte.

39
00:02:25,606 --> 00:02:27,841
Toh key ko bhi code mein mat likho.

40
00:02:29,141 --> 00:02:33,511
Hamesha ki tarah, ek fresh
virtual environment se shuru karo.

41
00:02:33,861 --> 00:02:36,282
Phir anthropic package install karo.

42
00:02:36,502 --> 00:02:41,736
Mai version two point three point zero
pin kar rahi hoon, jis version par yeh course

43
00:02:41,736 --> 00:02:42,671
record hua hai.

44
00:02:42,891 --> 00:02:49,255
SDK ka matlab hai software development
kit, yaani ready made Python code jo API se

45
00:02:49,255 --> 00:02:51,738
baat karna aasaan bana deta hai.

46
00:02:52,088 --> 00:02:53,831
Aur apni key set karo.

47
00:02:54,051 --> 00:02:59,314
Windows PowerShell par dollar
env colon ANTHROPIC API KEY use karo.

48
00:02:59,534 --> 00:03:02,853
Ya Module 1 ki tarah
dot env file mein rakho.

49
00:03:04,153 --> 00:03:06,678
Ek honest note, demos ke baare mein.

50
00:03:06,898 --> 00:03:12,717
Taaki har demo free ho aur har baar same
result de, aur aap bina key ke bhi follow

51
00:03:12,717 --> 00:03:18,678
kar sako, aap jo replies dekhoge woh iss
project ke ek chhote fake API se aate hain.

52
00:03:18,898 --> 00:03:25,521
Yeh fake API real API wala hi protocol
bolta hai, isliye real SDK code bilkul waise

53
00:03:25,521 --> 00:03:26,638
hi chalta hai.

54
00:03:26,858 --> 00:03:32,125
Lekin replies placeholders hain, jin
par likha hota hai offline demo reply.

55
00:03:32,345 --> 00:03:34,456
Yeh model ka output nahi hai.

56
00:03:34,676 --> 00:03:38,492
Key set karoge, toh yahi
code seedhe Claude se baat karega.

57
00:03:39,792 --> 00:03:41,598
Ab how: pehli request.

58
00:03:41,818 --> 00:03:45,814
Left side par code hai,
right side par uska real output.

59
00:03:46,034 --> 00:03:47,895
Line by line chalte hain.

60
00:03:48,245 --> 00:03:50,116
Pehle client banta hai.

61
00:03:50,336 --> 00:03:56,379
Apne projects mein aap anthropic dot
Anthropic likhoge, jo environment se key padh

62
00:03:56,379 --> 00:03:57,042
leta hai.

63
00:03:57,262 --> 00:04:02,769
Hamara lesson helper bhi wahi karta hai
jab key set ho, aur key na ho toh offline

64
00:04:02,769 --> 00:04:04,060
fake use karta hai.

65
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:07,408
Messages dot create request bhejta hai.

66
00:04:07,628 --> 00:04:09,680
Teen arguments zaroori hain.

67
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:11,991
Model, yaani kaunsa model.

68
00:04:12,211 --> 00:04:16,594
Max tokens, yaani reply
maximum kitna lamba ho sakta hai.

69
00:04:16,814 --> 00:04:19,790
Aur messages, yaani conversation ki list.

70
00:04:20,010 --> 00:04:24,361
Har message ek dictionary hai,
jisme role aur content hota hai.

71
00:04:24,581 --> 00:04:28,183
Bilkul wahi shape jo
aapne Module 1 mein banayi thi.

72
00:04:28,533 --> 00:04:31,436
Reply ka content ek list hai, blocks ki.

73
00:04:31,656 --> 00:04:36,270
Yahan ek hi text block hai,
isliye hum uska text print karte hain.

74
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:40,803
Right side par pehli line yahi
hai: offline placeholder reply.

75
00:04:41,153 --> 00:04:43,743
Yeh line stop reason print karti hai.

76
00:04:43,963 --> 00:04:49,417
Output mein end turn aaya, matlab
model ne apna answer naturally khatam kiya.

77
00:04:49,767 --> 00:04:52,581
Aur aakhri line tokens print karti hai.

78
00:04:52,801 --> 00:04:56,006
Nau tokens gaye,
chausath tokens wapas aaye.

79
00:04:56,226 --> 00:04:59,557
Usage hi woh cheez hai
jiska aapko bill aata hai.

80
00:05:00,857 --> 00:05:03,182
Ab response ko kholke dekhte hain.

81
00:05:03,402 --> 00:05:05,955
ID har response ka unique number hai.

82
00:05:06,175 --> 00:05:09,860
Koi problem report karni
ho, toh yeh ID batate hain.

83
00:05:10,210 --> 00:05:14,054
Model batata hai kaunse
model ne actually answer diya.

84
00:05:14,404 --> 00:05:17,732
Content mein answer hai,
blocks ki list ki form mein.

85
00:05:18,082 --> 00:05:23,244
Stop reason batata hai answer
complete hua, cut off hua, ya refuse hua.

86
00:05:23,594 --> 00:05:26,971
Aur usage batata hai
kitne tokens gaye aur aaye.

87
00:05:27,191 --> 00:05:30,334
Production code isse
hamesha record karta hai.

88
00:05:30,554 --> 00:05:32,686
Project mein hum yahi karenge.

89
00:05:33,986 --> 00:05:35,665
Content list kyun hai?

90
00:05:35,885 --> 00:05:39,943
Kyunki ek reply mein alag
alag type ke blocks ho sakte hain.

91
00:05:40,163 --> 00:05:42,906
Text block mein likha hua answer hota hai.

92
00:05:43,256 --> 00:05:46,483
Thinking block mein model
ki reasoning ho sakti hai.

93
00:05:46,703 --> 00:05:52,003
Current models par yeh by default hidden
hoti hai, lekin block wahan ho sakta hai.

94
00:05:52,353 --> 00:05:56,809
Aur tool use block ek request
hai ki aapka koi tool chalaya jaaye.

95
00:05:57,029 --> 00:05:59,504
Agents isi tarah kaam karte hain.

96
00:05:59,724 --> 00:06:01,739
Yeh Module 5 mein aayega.

97
00:06:02,089 --> 00:06:07,193
Isliye achha code yeh assume nahi
karta ki pehla block hamesha text hai.

98
00:06:07,413 --> 00:06:09,840
Woh har block ka type check karta hai.

99
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:12,460
Agla example yahi dikhata hai.

100
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:15,258
Ab system prompt.

101
00:06:15,478 --> 00:06:18,780
Isse ek shift se pehle
ki briefing ki tarah socho.

102
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:24,625
Manager naye employee ko batata hai: tum
kaun ho, rules kya hain, aur customers se

103
00:06:24,625 --> 00:06:26,065
kaise baat karni hai.

104
00:06:26,285 --> 00:06:30,220
System prompt wahi briefing
hai, poori conversation ke liye.

105
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:35,006
System parameter model
ko role aur rules deta hai.

106
00:06:35,226 --> 00:06:37,991
Yeh messages list ke bahar hota hai.

107
00:06:38,211 --> 00:06:43,417
Yahan rule hai: patient tutor bano,
aur maximum do sentences mein answer do.

108
00:06:43,767 --> 00:06:49,123
Aur yeh answer padhne ka safe tareeka
hai: har block par loop karo, aur sirf text

109
00:06:49,123 --> 00:06:50,313
blocks print karo.

110
00:06:50,533 --> 00:06:54,981
Offline mode mein placeholder
instructions follow nahi kar sakta.

111
00:06:55,201 --> 00:06:58,265
Real model do sentences mein answer deta.

112
00:06:58,485 --> 00:07:01,068
Prompt design par poora Module 3 hai.

113
00:07:02,368 --> 00:07:03,827
Interview corner.

114
00:07:04,047 --> 00:07:08,285
Sabse basic, lekin sabse
common question: API kya hai?

115
00:07:10,635 --> 00:07:17,020
Ek achha answer: API ek defined tareeka
hai jisse ek program doosre program se kuch

116
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:17,866
maang sake.

117
00:07:18,086 --> 00:07:23,338
Aap ek agreed format mein request
bhejte ho, aur response wapas aata hai.

118
00:07:23,558 --> 00:07:26,435
Waiter wali analogy bhi bol sakte ho.

119
00:07:26,655 --> 00:07:30,009
Trap: API ko library ya website mat bolna.

120
00:07:30,229 --> 00:07:33,396
API dono programs ke
beech ka contract hai.

121
00:07:33,746 --> 00:07:38,068
Doosra question: API keys ko
code se bahar kaise rakhte ho?

122
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:45,034
Answer: environment variables
mein, ya kisi secrets manager mein.

123
00:07:45,254 --> 00:07:47,123
Source code mein kabhi nahi.

124
00:07:47,343 --> 00:07:50,801
Har app ki alag key, aur
leak hote hi key revoke karo.

125
00:07:51,021 --> 00:07:53,971
Trap: config file
mein repo ke andar rakhna.

126
00:07:54,191 --> 00:07:57,108
Git mein jo bhi gaya, usse public samjho.

127
00:07:58,408 --> 00:07:59,665
Practice time.

128
00:07:59,885 --> 00:08:02,361
Video pause karo aur khud try karo.

129
00:08:02,711 --> 00:08:07,357
Pehla: messages dot create ke
teen zaroori arguments kaun se hain?

130
00:08:07,707 --> 00:08:12,839
Doosra: first call dot py ko badlo,
taaki woh har block ka type print kare.

131
00:08:13,189 --> 00:08:17,576
Teesra: agent mein content
zero dot text likhna risky kyun hai?

132
00:08:17,926 --> 00:08:21,910
Aur scenario: aapke teammate
ne ek key GitHub par push kar di.

133
00:08:22,130 --> 00:08:24,488
Aap kya karoge, order mein batao.

134
00:08:30,838 --> 00:08:35,068
Hint for the last one: pehla
step hai key ko turant revoke karna.

135
00:08:35,288 --> 00:08:38,263
Git history se hata dena kaafi nahi hai.

136
00:08:39,563 --> 00:08:40,491
Quick check.

137
00:08:40,711 --> 00:08:45,128
Messages dot create ke liye
kaun se teen arguments zaroori hain?

138
00:08:50,828 --> 00:08:53,292
Model, max tokens, aur messages.

139
00:08:53,512 --> 00:08:57,523
Key environment se aati hai,
aur system prompt optional hai.

140
00:08:58,823 --> 00:08:59,663
Recap.

141
00:08:59,883 --> 00:09:03,347
API aapke code aur
model ke beech ka waiter hai.

142
00:09:03,697 --> 00:09:07,810
Keys environment variable mein
rehti hain, code mein kabhi nahi.

143
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:13,079
Messages dot create ko model,
max tokens, aur messages chahiye.

144
00:09:13,429 --> 00:09:17,903
Response mein content blocks,
stop reason, aur usage milta hai.

145
00:09:18,253 --> 00:09:20,536
Agle lesson mein conversations.

146
00:09:20,756 --> 00:09:26,369
Aap khud dekhoge ki model bhoolta kyun
hai, aur message history ko sahi tareeke se

147
00:09:26,369 --> 00:09:28,012
kaise manage karte hain.
